WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.870
Who was behind the coup in Turkey? At this
point, there's three main conspiracies which

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:16.270
are out there. President Erdogan is blaming
Fethullah Gulen, a former ally turned rival

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:22.110
who's an Islamic cleric who's an exile in
Pennsylvania. He wants him extradited. He

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:27.360
says that his followers in the police force
in the military were behind this attempt to

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.750
oust his democratically elected government.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:36.110
However, the Turkish military has traditionally
been the domain of the Kemalists, the followers

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:41.870
of Mustafa Kemal Ataturk, the founder of modern
Turkey. They're staunch secularists; they

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:47.190
hate Fethullah Gulen. And now that the Erdogan
government has also accused the former head

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:52.730
of the air force, General Ozturk, it seems
unlikely that he would ever be a Gulen-ist.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:56.670
The other possibility, of course, is that
Erdogan's followers himself staged this as

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:02.940
a sort of Reichstag fire. One of the generals
arrested, Mehmet Disli, is actually the brother

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:09.950
of the AKP's vice president. We're not going
to know for a long time who was behind this.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.179
So who was behind the coup? Will we ever know?
Let us know in the comments below and let

00:01:15.179 --> 00:01:19.229
us know any other topics you’d like AEI
scholars to cover in 60 Seconds.

